STATUS: Generate one standalone, reusable Orc boss landmark for Urkaaaz's
campaign maps. Base its design on the boss markers at levels 5 and 10 in the
newest attached campaign-map screenshot. This is a transparent map overlay,
not a map, screenshot, or gameplay character sprite.

## Reference input

- Attach the newest campaign-map screenshot showing the boss landmarks at
  levels 5 and 10. Use those two markers as the primary reference for the
  boss silhouette, skull, horns, banners, and compact shrine-like base.
- Attach the approved blue-banner fortress marker only as a secondary
  reference for matching painterly materials, navy cloth, ivory skull
  emblems, and restrained amber lighting. The boss must remain visibly
  different from a regular fortress.
- The newest campaign-map screenshot supersedes older placeholder boss art.
  Treat its map, route, level plaques, numbers, locks, and selection glow as
  separate visual layers; do not copy them into the asset.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG:
  `campaign_map_marker_boss.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/map-markers/`.
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 512 pixels, square, RGBA.
- Use genuine transparent alpha. Do not draw a checkerboard or any opaque or
  colored canvas.
- Center the complete boss landmark and keep it within the central 82% of the
  canvas, with clean transparent margins on every side.
- Generate one reusable boss marker for both chapter boss locations, not a
  sprite sheet, contact sheet, or collection of variants.

## Boss landmark design

- Depict a compact, unmistakable Orc boss shrine/stronghold, viewed from the
  same elevated three-quarter angle as the boss markers in the screenshot.
- Make a large ivory horned skull the dominant focal point. Give it a
  powerful, readable silhouette with deep eye sockets, heavy tusks or horns,
  and a few bold bone details.
- Set the skull into a squat, broad base of rough charcoal stone and dark
  timber with a reinforced gate or spiked palisade details. Keep it lower and
  more skull-centered than the tall, tower-dominant fortress marker.
- Add small deep-navy banners with simple ivory skull emblems. Use restrained
  amber light in eye sockets, windows, or attached torches to match the
  screenshot's warm firelit style.
- Use weathered stone, near-black timber, iron, bone ivory, navy cloth, and
  limited torch amber. Keep the finish painterly, high-contrast, and
  consistent with the approved fortress marker without copying its silhouette.
- At 48 dp display size, the horned skull must remain the clearest feature;
  simplify minor architecture instead of shrinking the skull or adding tiny
  details.
- Keep the object centered, upright, biome-neutral, and legible over both
  bright and dark campaign-map terrain.

## Separation from UI and other assets

- Generate only the boss illustration. Android draws the level number,
  marker hit target, lock/check status, and selection feedback separately.
- Do not draw a circular or hexagonal badge, marker frame, status ring,
  pedestal, selection glow, lock, checkmark, number plaque, level number,
  label, text, or other UI.
- Do not draw a map, terrain tile, path, biome background, separate scenery,
  surrounding city, soldiers, weapons, or battle effects.
- Do not depict a full-body boss character, attack pose, projectile, or combat
  scene. This is a campaign landmark icon, not the in-match boss unit.
- Do not add a large cast shadow, smoke, flames, or light rays outside the
  landmark silhouette. Keep transparent pixels clean and attached to the art.
- The fortress marker is a separate asset. Do not turn this boss into a
  standard tower keep or reuse the fortress silhouette.

## Negative prompt

background, opaque background, colored background, checkerboard, map, terrain,
grass tile, path, biome scenery, sky, water, sprite sheet, multiple icons,
side-view gameplay character, full-body boss, attack pose, battle scene,
human knight, human castle, ordinary fortress keep, tall tower-dominant
fortress, plain human skull, tiny unreadable details, polished white stone,
crimson banners, red roof, heraldic shield, fleur-de-lis, sprawling city,
fortress complex, ornate filigree, soldiers, creatures, weapons, combat,
projectiles, explosions, smoke, text, letters, numbers, labels, logo,
watermark, signature, badge, circular frame, hexagonal frame, marker pin,
status ring, selection glow, level plaque, lock, checkmark, UI, cropped horns,
cropped skull, detached shadow, colored fringe, jagged alpha edges

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly one centered boss landmark is present on a 512 x 512 RGBA
  canvas with genuine transparency.
- Preview at 48 dp and confirm the horned skull remains immediately
  recognizable and distinct from the fortress marker.
- Confirm the art matches the boss landmarks at levels 5 and 10 in the newest
  screenshot and uses its navy-banner, ivory, and amber palette.
- Confirm no badge, plaque, number, status, lock, text, map, character pose,
  or separate scenery is baked into the image.
- Confirm the silhouette contrasts against both light and dark map regions.
- Do not import the generated image into Android until it is reviewed and
  approved. Once approved, it can replace the boss vector placeholder without
  changing map anchors or progression logic.
